        "original_id": "c5d60196-313b-5b73-8994-623d7c33dfc9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Samuel Fereday Smith; Francis Egerton, 3rd Duke of Bridgewater\n- Organizations: Bridgewater Trustees\n- Roles: Deputy Superintendent; canal manager; industrialist\n- Places: Worsley; Manchester\n- Systems: Bridgewater Canal\n\nFacts:\n- George Samuel Fereday Smith was born on 7 May 1812 and died on 26 May 1891.\n- George Samuel Fereday Smith was an English industrialist and canal manager.\n- From 1837 to 1887, George Samuel Fereday Smith served as Deputy Superintendent of the Bridgewater Trustees and their successors.\n- The Bridgewater Trustees and their successors derived their major source of income from the Bridgewater Canal.\n- Francis Egerton, 3rd Duke of Bridgewater, commissioned the Bridgewater Canal to transport coal from his mines in Worsley to Manchester.",
